## Pointers (from the dotnet report)
`framework/languages/cpp/framework/src/runtime/mesh/raw_mesh_node_owner.cpp:3863-3885` starts admission on the READY edge without a seal check; `:2897-2908`
answers a duplicate admission with Admit only (no completion diagnostic). Find the cpp host's shutdown seal owner (drain/admission gate equivalent of dotnet
`ZLinkDrainAdmissionGate`) and how Relocate's Draining differs from the shutdown seal (must not be confused).

## Fix (single owner each; rule count before/after)
1. Seal → mesh: the mesh node reads the existing host shutdown seal (no new flag) before submitting a Hello; sealed → no Hello for Connecting peers, Draining
   Update to admitted peers continues; the peer-loss transitions (disconnect, liveness expiry, send failure) keep Draining after the seal (one state rule).
2. Duplicate/idempotent admission: same completion diagnostic (the log/flow event the ZoneWorld runner reads) as Accept; no duplicate PeerAdmitted event.
3. Tests: unit (a) sealed node + peer loss → no Hello, stays Draining, drain completes; (b) unsealed still re-admits; (c) crossed Hello/Admit both sides emit the
   completion diagnostic. Then `bash samples/run_samples.sh` once (7/7 + self-checks) and the cpp unit ctest.

